  <sys:String x:Key="Retouch_LimitsTitle">What it can and cannot do</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Retouch_LimitText">Smart fill rebuilds from surrounding pixels and works best on solid or gradient backgrounds. On textured areas (grass, fabric, faces) it leaves smooth patches — use the clone stamp there instead.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Retouch_HowHeal">Smart fill: enter the mode, drag a rectangle over what to remove (repeat as needed), then click “Smart fill”.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Retouch_HowClone">Clone stamp: enter the mode, Alt-click to set the source, then paint elsewhere.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Retouch_UndoHint">Both can be undone with Ctrl+Z. Each stroke only stores the pixels of the changed region, so memory use stays low.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_Tab">Annotate</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_Title">Annotations (non-destructive)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_Intro">Annotations are objects layered over the image: you can select, recolor, move and delete them at any time without touching the pixels. They are baked into the image only when you export or print — and automatically before any destructive operation such as a filter or crop.</sys:String>
