  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_CoverBlur">Blur (good for faces and backgrounds)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_CoverStrength">Strength</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_CoverHint">Larger blocks / radius hide more. Mosaic blocks are anchored to the image grid, so they do not drift while you drag the annotation.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_Delete">Delete selected</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_ClearAll">Clear all</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_Flatten">Bake into image</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_HowTo">How to use</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_Step1">1. Click “Enter annotate mode” and pick a type.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_Step2">2. Drag on the canvas to draw. Number badges and text just need a click.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_Step3">3. Click an annotation to select it. Color, stroke width and font size apply immediately; drag to move it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_Step4">4. A selected annotation shows 8 white handles: drag them to resize (Shift keeps the aspect ratio, Alt resizes from the center). For text, dragging a corner changes the font size.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_Step5">5. Covers (mosaic / blur) are sampled from the image and recomputed live while dragging; they are written into the pixels only on export or bake.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Annotation_UndoHint">Every step can be undone with Ctrl+Z (the history stores object-list snapshots, which are very cheap).</sys:String>
